WEBVTT

NOTE enable-disable-stations: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.452
Take a station, hole or
area out of adjustment,

V0-2
00:00:05.552 --> 00:00:08.830
and understand what cascading
does before you confirm it.

V1a-1
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.820
The switch in the Enable column
takes effect on that station alone.

V1b-1
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.624
Station 5AP1 is off here,

V1b-2
00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:25.220
which is why it has no pending
adjustment however dry it reads.

V2a-1
00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:35.707
Hole and area rows carry the same
switch. Turning one off takes

V2a-2
00:00:35.807 --> 00:00:39.774
everything beneath it out of the push
and off the Enabled Stations map,

V2a-3
00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:42.277
but leaves their own
switches as they were.

V2b-1
00:00:44.653 --> 00:00:47.823
Hold Shift as you click to switch
everything beneath it off too.

V3a-1
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:58.039
Because a cascade can affect dozens
of heads, Spatial Adjust asks

V3a-2
00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:02.190
first and names the scope: this
hole and every station beneath it.

V3b-1
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:07.897
Continue applies it; Cancel
leaves everything as it was.

V4a-1
00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:20.384
The checkbox suppresses the confirmation
for future cascades. It is stored in your

V4a-2
00:01:20.484 --> 00:01:24.943
own preferences, so it hides the prompt
for you and not for your colleagues.

V4b-1
00:01:27.257 --> 00:01:32.161
Careful: with the prompt suppressed,
a Shift-click on an area switch changes

V4b-2
00:01:32.261 --> 00:01:37.617
every hole and station under it at once,
with only a footer message to show for it.

V5a-1
00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:48.523
Switch Layers to Enabled Stations to
see only the heads still in adjustment.

V5b-1
00:01:50.887 --> 00:01:53.957
Anything that disappeared is out,
deliberately or otherwise.
